    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st period",
        "score": "MTL 2, BOS 0",
        "text": "Kirby Dach scored on a wraparound 2:34 in, and Josh Anderson batted a rebound out of the air at 8:36 after Jake Evans deflected Mike Matheson's shot. Montreal hasn't trailed after a first period this season."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd period",
        "score": "MTL 5, BOS 1",
        "text": "Evans scored on a breakaway backhand off Anderson's stretch pass at 4:24, and Cole Caufield took the puck off David Pastrnak and scored on another breakaway at 8:14 for 4–0, ending Swayman's night after four goals on 17 shots. Phillip Danault's one-timer off Michael DiPietro made it 5–0 at 14:15; 38 seconds later, Casey Mittelstadt scored on a breakaway backhand to end Jacob Fowler's shutout bid."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd period",
        "score": "Final: MTL 5, BOS 2",
        "text": "Mittelstadt scored again 52 seconds in, on a rebound of an Elias Lindholm shot, for 5–2. Montreal's Chris Kreider left at 6:27 after an open-ice collision with Mikey Eyssimont and didn't return. Boston outshot Montreal 32–31 for the game."
      }
    ],
